; SELinux policy module for razerd-battery.service (Fedora/RHEL targeted policy).
;
; The unit gets its /dev/uhid descriptor from the service manager (OpenFile=),
; which opens the node while still in systemd's own domain, init_t — and the
; stock policy has no rule letting init_t read/write uhid_device_t. This adds
; exactly that — the three permissions an O_RDWR open() is checked against
; (`read write` on the inode, then `open` on the file), nothing else. It widens nothing in practice: init_t is PID 1, and handing a
; unit an OpenFile= already requires root.
;
; Install: semodule -i razerd-uhid.cil      Remove: semodule -r razerd-uhid
(allow init_t uhid_device_t (chr_file (open read write)))
